<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Danture</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1594</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinhalese-portuguese-war">Sinhalese–Portuguese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Danture was fought in 1594 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, where King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vimaladharmasuriya-i">Vimaladharmasuriya I</a> of Kandy destroyed a Portuguese army under Pedro Lopes de Sousa that had come to install a client queen, Dona Catarina. The Portuguese commander was killed, and Vimaladharmasuriya married Dona Catarina, securing his throne and Kandy's independence.</p></div>
